un, **then** the forged-artifact, cross-claim, same-claim, across-restart replay, and crash-mid-mint fixtures are each rejected by the spine.\n\n## Wave 25 â€” Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation (E1b)\n**Deliverables:** the deterministic SCORER computing **Metric G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the **SCORED SUBSET** (the canonical token, used identically here and in DESCRIPTION Â§Residuals: the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and supplies ONLY the false-positive-rate / kâ€² term); the PINNED canned baseline (two stub scorers: always-ABSTAIN AND always-FLAG, scored on the SCORED SUBSET, G computed identically); the ABLATION arm.\n**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part A: fixture corpus + red-team set\n**done-when (cites the pinned constants):** **G(battery-on) > G(better-stub-baseline) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **per-class catch floors met** â€” derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%, convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset**; **ABSTAIN-correctness = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN.\n- **Given** the ablation arm (battery disabled), **when** the scorer runs on the SCORED SUBSET, **then** G drops below battery-on by more than 0.30 (battery is load-bearing).\n- **Given** either stub baseline, **when** the scorer runs, **then** battery-on G exceeds the better stub's G by > 0.30, and all per-class floors + kâ€² + the 100% abstain floor hold (else the wave HALTs).\n\n## Wave 26 â€” Journal integration (E2)\n**Deliverables:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep-loop input feeding the oracle's fixture-failure learning.\n**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation\n**done-when:** a run appends a 7-field journal entry and the sleep-loop consumes it (tested).\n- **Given** a completed run, **when** journal integration executes, **then** a well-formed 7-field entry is appended and the sleep-loop reads it.\n\n## Wave 27 â€” Author SKILL.md (full) + invocation smoke test (E3) â€” project-DONE\n**Deliverables:** the full tiered-scope SKILL.md headline; the per-pillar usage contract; the explicit Increment-1 acceptance note (\"NS abstain-arms DONE; NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 positive-arm = Increment-2\"); the invocation smoke test; the 5-gate productionization checklist.\n**Depends on:** Journal integration\n**done-when:** an invocation smoke test (a canned input) produces a correctly-stamped abstain/route through the REAL router; the SKILL.md states the Increment-1 acceptance boundary; the 5-gate productionization checklist + manifest checker pass.\n- **Given** a canned proof-bearing input, **when** the skill is invoked end-to-end, **then** it returns a CONJECTURAL+routed result with an honest per-claim rung+verifier-family stamp + advisory payload, and the SKILL.md headline declares NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 as Increment-2.\n","numLines":178,"startLine":1,"totalLines":178}}}
