{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SfLrke6KsHJFoBiTcPTvh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Ramanujan â€” Description (v3, post Stage-2 round 2)\n2\t\n3\t**North Star:** Ramanujan = a 6-pillar mathematical-reasoning PARTNER (Understand/Solve/Verify/Dialogue/Formalize/Contextualize) on ONE shared claim-ledger + verify-router spine, governed by THE HONESTY LAW (no same-family-authored object reaches a VERIFIED rung; the autonomous tier settles only literal finite computations bound to a re-executable out-of-model SUBPROCESS artifact; everything else ABSTAINS + routes to an out-of-model certifier). NS1â€“NS9.\n4\t\n5\t## What this build is\n6\tThe AUTONOMOUS increment (Phases Aâ€“E, Waves 1â€“27) of Ramanujan, buildable on the bare single-family subscription: the shared spine (typed claim ledger + the re-executable adjudication-artifact substrate + the Honesty-Law canary suite + the always-on VERIFY router + the default-deny autonomous-VERIFIED gate), the six pillars in their autonomous form, and the gradeable oracle + journal + the full SKILL.md. Honest degradation is the design.\n7\t\n8\t## INCREMENT-1 ACCEPTANCE BOUNDARY (explicit)\n9\tNS3-routing-lift, NS4-faithfulness, and NS7-human-gate are STRUCTURALLY UNVERIFIABLE in this increment and realized ONLY as their honest abstain+route arm. Their positive arm is the promotion-gated Increment-2 (below). **Project-DONE @ Wave 27 = \"NS abstain-arms DONE; NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 positive-arm = Increment-2\" â€” NOT \"NS1â€“9 satisfied.\"** The only positive VERIFIED lift Increment-1 demonstrates is the A4 literal-computation path (NS9/NS3-computational).\n10\t\n11\t## Success criteria\n12\tNS1 verified laddered comprehension Â· NS2 generative SOLVE + executable CONTROL Â· NS3 always-on independent VERIFY router + honest abstain (positive lift = Increment-2) Â· NS4 autoformalization faithfulness (Increment-2; abstain-arm here) Â· NS5 honest per-claim rung+verifier-family stamp Â· NS6 stateful DIALOGUE that never asserts unverified math as settled Â· NS7 interactive FORMALIZE + human gate (Increment-2; abstain-stub here) Â· NS8 CONTEXTUALIZE composes researchPrime/Gandalf without reimplementing Â· NS9 THE HONESTY LAW (canaries + gradeable oracle).\n13\t\n14\t## Honesty stamps (from Stage-1 convergence)\n15\t`cross_model:false verified:true` (single-family Sharks/Judge). Single-family ceiling = CLAIMED on proof/conceptual claims; CBS register FLAGGED, not mitigated. Autonomous-VERIFIED = re-execution-backed literal computation only; single-process forgery-resistance is best-effort (the warrant is the canary's out-of-band re-execution, not an in-process key).\n16\t\n17\t## Â§Build-host & subprocess contract (win32)\n18\t- **Test gate:** `node --test test/` per wave; no shell, no PowerShell (the host has no pwsh).\n19\t- **P9 firewall subprocess:** the sandbox is a child **`node <test/sandbox-runner.mjs>`** invoked via `child_process.execFile('node', [...])` (NOT a shell), the literal-computation AST passed as a JSON arg/stdin, evaluated over **EXACT arithmetic (bigint/rational, NO float)** so re-execution is deterministic by construction. Each invocation uses a **hermetic temp dir** `path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'ramanujan-fw-' + nonce)` created+removed per call. **Re-execution** = the canary re-runs the same child on the same input and compares a SHA-256 of canonical (sorted-key, exact-number) stdout. Artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` where runtime_fingerprint = `{node_major, canonicalization_version}` (reproduced or recorded so a version skew is detected, not silently hashed-around).\n20\t- **Inherited modules:** resolved via a pinned **`inherits.manifest.json`** (repo root) mapping each logical name â†’ resolvable path + expected exports (Phase-0 handoff/journal/sleep; Gandalf v1 commission seam; the three dive engines). The Wave-2 A0.5a gate reads it and fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry. Authoring the manifest is the first deliverable of Wave 2 (its terminus-acceptance artifact).\n21\t\n22\t## Â§Residuals â€” REQUIRED-BEFORE-BUILD, PINNED (value Â· owner Â· terminus-acceptance)\n23\t- **A0.5a (inheritance gate)** â€” *value:* `inherits.manifest.json` + a `node --test` resolving/version/interface-shape-checking each entry. *Owner:* Wave 2. *Terminus:* green test; fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry.\n24\t- **R1 (oracle roster + per-class k + kâ€² + FP tolerance)** â€” *value:* 6 planted-defect classes (derivation-error, dimensional, off-by-one, convergence-stability, comprehension-narrative, firewall-inapplicable) Ã— â‰¥3 instances; a FIXED **6-fixture SOUND subset** (separate from the iâ€“xiv union, used ONLY for the false-positive / kâ€² term and EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator); per-class catch floors: **derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%**, **convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each**; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset** (absolute integer). *kâ€² and the Metric-G false-positive-rate intentionally share the SOUND-subset cardinality (kâ€² = count form, G FP-rate = rate form of the same observations), so that cardinality is a single load-bearing constant.* Numeric-anchor FP tolerance = relative 1e-9. *Owner:* Wave 24 (corpus) + Wave 25 (scoring). *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when asserts all per-class floors + kâ€².\n25\t- **Metric G + canned baseline (the oracle gate)** â€” *value:* **G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the canonical **SCORED SUBSET** (= the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and feeds only the FP/kâ€² term â€” the SAME token is used verbatim in the Wave-25 done-when). The canned baseline is PINNED as TWO stub scorers â€” **always-ABSTAIN** and **always-FLAG** â€” scored on the identical SCORED SUBSET with G computed by the identical formula; **acceptance = G(battery-on) > G(better stub) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **ABSTAIN-correctness floor = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN. *Owner:* Wave 25. *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when cites the SCORED SUBSET token, the two stub baselines, the 0.30 epsilon, the per-class floors, kâ€², and the 100% abstain floor.\n26\t- **S1 (CONTROL thresholds + gap-function)** â€” *value:* budget = 8 steps; gap-function = no progress-boolean=true in the last m=3 steps â‡’ switch; 2 consecutive switches â‡’ ABANDON; on the pinned canned non-converging fixture ABANDON fires via the gap-function **strictly before step 8** (reason=gap-function, never budget-exhausted). *Owner:* Wave 17. *Terminus:* the ABANDON fixture exits reason=gap-function before step 8, claim left UNVERIFIED.\n27\t- **S4 (ref-fn-independence invariant)** â€” *value:* a firewall ref-fn whose AST shares no symbol-provenance with the comprehension narrative; else cap at CLAIMED. *Owner:* Wave 11. *Terminus:* the planted-wrong-same-family-reference fixture caps at CLAIMED.\n28\t- **P3 (example-space-stability predicate)** â€” *value:* ADVISORY-only; \"stable\" = no new monster in the last r=2 example-rounds; never gates promotion. *Owner:* Wave 20. *Terminus:* a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F.\n29\t- **P7 (default-deny grammar + battery + recall roster + closure)** â€” *value:* a CLOSED whitelist grammar over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; NO float/symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); â‰¥8 positive-recall computations (incl. â‰¥1 nested-composition) it MUST settle; â‰¥8 smuggled-non-literal inputs (incl. â‰¥1 deep-nested-smuggle) it MUST reject. *Owner:* Wave 8 (grammar+battery) + Wave 9 (recall) + Waves 24/25 (scored). *Terminus:* 100% reject on the battery AND 100% settle on the recall roster, closure-tested.\n30\t- **P9 (provenance-binding contract)** â€” *value:* artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` from the Wave-9 subprocess [/ .olean / SMT cert in Increment-2]; canary re-execution = re-run the subprocess and compare the SHA-256 stdout hash; freshness = a **single-use claim-bound nonce = hash(claim_id + domain + monotone-counter)** where the monotone-counter is **DURABLE + monotone across restarts** (last-issued value per (claim_id,domain) persisted to the Phase-0 durability substrate â€” reuse, no new store; acceptable alt: a high-entropy per-mint random nonce + a persisted spent-nonce set the canary checks). **Write-ordering:** the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE the artifact becomes valid, so a crash after mint but before flush leaves no usable replayable nonce on restart. Wave 2 round-trips the durable counter/spent-set across a simulated reload before Wave 4 relies on it. *Owner:* Wave 4 (+ Wave 2 substrate round-trip, Wave 6, Waves 24/25). *Terminus:* the E1 forged-artifact, cross-claim-replay, same-claim-replay, across-restart-replay, AND crash-mid-mint attempts are all rejected.\n31\t- **P8 (SMT/cross-family integrity)** â€” *Increment-2 (Phase F).* *Value:* probabilistic-class integrity = N=5 trials at temp=0; pass-threshold = 5/5 reject of a known-FALSE sentinel + 5/5 accept of a known-true; under-threshold â‡’ capped at CORROBORATED-degraded + quarantine. *Owner:* Increment-2 F0/F3. *Terminus:* a stubbed/wrong certifier is empirically quarantined (not merely flagged).\n32\t\n33\t## Increment-2 (HALT-gated â€” North-Star Phase F; NOT in this wave list)\n34\tBuild ONLY on explicit user promotion, after an F0 environment liveness + per-class integrity probe passes: **F0** environment probe Â· **F1** cross-family MODEL verifier (â†’ CORROBORATED) Â· **F2** Lean toolchain (â†’ OBSERVED) Â· **F3** SMT-roundtrip faithfulness certifier Â· **F4** autonomous commission DISPATCH + silent intent-classification Â· **F5** the human gate + cross-family GROUNDED-rung promotion. Until promoted, the VERIFY router ABSTAINS to these and stamps the gap. The full pinned Phase-F plan is the next Crucible/Foreman pass.\n35\t\n36\t## Provenance\n37\tGenerated by Crucible Stage 2 from the Stage-1 Master Plan (engine-converged 2026-06-21; `stage1/run/DELIVERABLE-ENGINE.json`), USER-approved, then vetted by the Stage-2 Shark-Tank loop (the v3 doc-trio absorbs Stage-2 rounds 1â€“2) and the well-formedness gate before handoff. North Star locked at `../NORTH-STAR-CANDIDATE-v3.md`.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f7f7d00-4235-48b9-9b7b-c7f241bb6c51","uuid":"f720ce31-f563-487e-b8e4-7fe59a20d94d","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:49:13.343Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\ramanujan\\planning\\crucible\\stage2\\handoff\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Ramanujan â€” Description (v3, post Stage-2 round 2)\n\n**North Star:** Ramanujan = a 6-pillar mathematical-reasoning PARTNER (Understand/Solve/Verify/Dialogue/Formalize/Contextualize) on ONE shared claim-ledger + verify-router spine, governed by THE HONESTY LAW (no same-family-authored object reaches a VERIFIED rung; the autonomous tier settles only literal finite computations bound to a re-executable out-of-model SUBPROCESS artifact; everything else ABSTAINS + routes to an out-of-model certifier). NS1â€“NS9.\n\n## What this build is\nThe AUTONOMOUS increment (Phases Aâ€“E, Waves 1â€“27) of Ramanujan, buildable on the bare single-family subscription: the shared spine (typed claim ledger + the re-executable adjudication-artifact substrate + the Honesty-Law canary suite + the always-on VERIFY router + the default-deny autonomous-VERIFIED gate), the six pillars in their autonomous form, and the gradeable oracle + journal + the full SKILL.md. Honest degradation is the design.\n\n## INCREMENT-1 ACCEPTANCE BOUNDARY (explicit)\nNS3-routing-lift, NS4-faithfulness, and NS7-human-gate are STRUCTURALLY UNVERIFIABLE in this increment and realized ONLY as their honest abstain+route arm. Their positive arm is the promotion-gated Increment-2 (below). **Project-DONE @ Wave 27 = \"NS abstain-arms DONE; NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 positive-arm = Increment-2\" â€” NOT \"NS1â€“9 satisfied.\"** The only positive VERIFIED lift Increment-1 demonstrates is the A4 literal-computation path (NS9/NS3-computational).\n\n## Success criteria\nNS1 verified laddered comprehension Â· NS2 generative SOLVE + executable CONTROL Â· NS3 always-on independent VERIFY router + honest abstain (positive lift = Increment-2) Â· NS4 autoformalization faithfulness (Increment-2; abstain-arm here) Â· NS5 honest per-claim rung+verifier-family stamp Â· NS6 stateful DIALOGUE that never asserts unverified math as settled Â· NS7 interactive FORMALIZE + human gate (Increment-2; abstain-stub here) Â· NS8 CONTEXTUALIZE composes researchPrime/Gandalf without reimplementing Â· NS9 THE HONESTY LAW (canaries + gradeable oracle).\n\n## Honesty stamps (from Stage-1 convergence)\n`cross_model:false verified:true` (single-family Sharks/Judge). Single-family ceiling = CLAIMED on proof/conceptual claims; CBS register FLAGGED, not mitigated. Autonomous-VERIFIED = re-execution-backed literal computation only; single-process forgery-resistance is best-effort (the warrant is the canary's out-of-band re-execution, not an in-process key).\n\n## Â§Build-host & subprocess contract (win32)\n- **Test gate:** `node --test test/` per wave; no shell, no PowerShell (the host has no pwsh).\n- **P9 firewall subprocess:** the sandbox is a child **`node <test/sandbox-runner.mjs>`** invoked via `child_process.execFile('node', [...])` (NOT a shell), the literal-computation AST passed as a JSON arg/stdin, evaluated over **EXACT arithmetic (bigint/rational, NO float)** so re-execution is deterministic by construction. Each invocation uses a **hermetic temp dir** `path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'ramanujan-fw-' + nonce)` created+removed per call. **Re-execution** = the canary re-runs the same child on the same input and compares a SHA-256 of canonical (sorted-key, exact-number) stdout. Artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` where runtime_fingerprint = `{node_major, canonicalization_version}` (reproduced or recorded so a version skew is detected, not silently hashed-around).\n- **Inherited modules:** resolved via a pinned **`inherits.manifest.json`** (repo root) mapping each logical name â†’ resolvable path + expected exports (Phase-0 handoff/journal/sleep; Gandalf v1 commission seam; the three dive engines). The Wave-2 A0.5a gate reads it and fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry. Authoring the manifest is the first deliverable of Wave 2 (its terminus-acceptance artifact).\n\n## Â§Residuals â€” REQUIRED-BEFORE-BUILD, PINNED (value Â· owner Â· terminus-acceptance)\n- **A0.5a (inheritance gate)** â€” *value:* `inherits.manifest.json` + a `node --test` resolving/version/interface-shape-checking each entry. *Owner:* Wave 2. *Terminus:* green test; fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry.\n- **R1 (oracle roster + per-class k + kâ€² + FP tolerance)** â€” *value:* 6 planted-defect classes (derivation-error, dimensional, off-by-one, convergence-stability, comprehension-narrative, firewall-inapplicable) Ã— â‰¥3 instances; a FIXED **6-fixture SOUND subset** (separate from the iâ€“xiv union, used ONLY for the false-positive / kâ€² term and EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator); per-class catch floors: **derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%**, **convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each**; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset** (absolute integer). *kâ€² and the Metric-G false-positive-rate intentionally share the SOUND-subset cardinality (kâ€² = count form, G FP-rate = rate form of the same observations), so that cardinality is a single load-bearing constant.* Numeric-anchor FP tolerance = relative 1e-9. *Owner:* Wave 24 (corpus) + Wave 25 (scoring). *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when asserts all per-class floors + kâ€².\n- **Metric G + canned baseline (the oracle gate)** â€” *value:* **G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the canonical **SCORED SUBSET** (= the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and feeds only the FP/kâ€² term â€” the SAME token is used verbatim in the Wave-25 done-when). The canned baseline is PINNED as TWO stub scorers â€” **always-ABSTAIN** and **always-FLAG** â€” scored on the identical SCORED SUBSET with G computed by the identical formula; **acceptance = G(battery-on) > G(better stub) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **ABSTAIN-correctness floor = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN. *Owner:* Wave 25. *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when cites the SCORED SUBSET token, the two stub baselines, the 0.30 epsilon, the per-class floors, kâ€², and the 100% abstain floor.\n- **S1 (CONTROL thresholds + gap-function)** â€” *value:* budget = 8 steps; gap-function = no progress-boolean=true in the last m=3 steps â‡’ switch; 2 consecutive switches â‡’ ABANDON; on the pinned canned non-converging fixture ABANDON fires via the gap-function **strictly before step 8** (reason=gap-function, never budget-exhausted). *Owner:* Wave 17. *Terminus:* the ABANDON fixture exits reason=gap-function before step 8, claim left UNVERIFIED.\n- **S4 (ref-fn-independence invariant)** â€” *value:* a firewall ref-fn whose AST shares no symbol-provenance with the comprehension narrative; else cap at CLAIMED. *Owner:* Wave 11. *Terminus:* the planted-wrong-same-family-reference fixture caps at CLAIMED.\n- **P3 (example-space-stability predicate)** â€” *value:* ADVISORY-only; \"stable\" = no new monster in the last r=2 example-rounds; never gates promotion. *Owner:* Wave 20. *Terminus:* a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F.\n- **P7 (default-deny grammar + battery + recall roster + closure)** â€” *value:* a CLOSED whitelist grammar over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; NO float/symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); â‰¥8 positive-recall computations (incl. â‰¥1 nested-composition) it MUST settle; â‰¥8 smuggled-non-literal inputs (incl. â‰¥1 deep-nested-smuggle) it MUST reject. *Owner:* Wave 8 (grammar+battery) + Wave 9 (recall) + Waves 24/25 (scored). *Terminus:* 100% reject on the battery AND 100% settle on the recall roster, closure-tested.\n- **P9 (provenance-binding contract)** â€” *value:* artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` from the Wave-9 subprocess [/ .olean / SMT cert in Increment-2]; canary re-execution = re-run the subprocess and compare the SHA-256 stdout hash; freshness = a **single-use claim-bound nonce = hash(claim_id + domain + monotone-counter)** where the monotone-counter is **DURABLE + monotone across restarts** (last-issued value per (claim_id,domain) persisted to the Phase-0 durability substrate â€” reuse, no new store; acceptable alt: a high-entropy per-mint random nonce + a persisted spent-nonce set the canary checks). **Write-ordering:** the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE the artifact becomes valid, so a crash after mint but before flush leaves no usable replayable nonce on restart. Wave 2 round-trips the durable counter/spent-set across a simulated reload before Wave 4 relies on it. *Owner:* Wave 4 (+ Wave 2 substrate round-trip, Wave 6, Waves 24/25). *Terminus:* the E1 forged-artifact, cross-claim-replay, same-claim-replay, across-restart-replay, AND crash-mid-mint attempts are all rejected.\n- **P8 (SMT/cross-family integrity)** â€” *Increment-2 (Phase F).* *Value:* probabilistic-class integrity = N=5 trials at temp=0; pass-threshold = 5/5 reject of a known-FALSE sentinel + 5/5 accept of a known-true; under-threshold â‡’ capped at CORROBORATED-degraded + quarantine. *Owner:* Increment-2 F0/F3. *Terminus:* a stubbed/wrong certifier is empirically quarantined (not merely flagged).\n\n## Increment-2 (HALT-gated â€” North-Star Phase F; NOT in this wave list)\nBuild ONLY on explicit user promotion, after an F0 environment liveness + per-class integrity probe passes: **F0** environment probe Â· **F1** cross-family MODEL verifier (â†’ CORROBORATED) Â· **F2** Lean toolchain (â†’ OBSERVED) Â· **F3** SMT-roundtrip faithfulness certifier Â· **F4** autonomous commission DISPATCH + silent intent-classification Â· **F5** the human gate + cross-family GROUNDED-rung promotion. Until promoted, the VERIFY router ABSTAINS to these and stamps the gap. The full pinned Phase-F plan is the next Crucible/Foreman pass.\n\n## Provenance\nGenerated by Crucible Stage 2 from the Stage-1 Master Plan (engine-converged 2026-06-21; `stage1/run/DELIVERABLE-ENGINE.json`), USER-approved, then vetted by the Stage-2 Shark-Tank loop (the v3 doc-trio absorbs Stage-2 rounds 1â€“2) and the well-formedness gate before handoff. North Star locked at `../NORTH-STAR-CANDIDATE-v3.md`.\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
