se-positive-rate** over the canonical SCORED SUBSET; acceptance (Wave 25): **G(battery-on) > G(better stub) + 0.30 strict**, ablation arm measurably lower, per-class catch floors (derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%; convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3), **kâ€² â‰¤ 1 false positive** on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset, and **100% ABSTAIN-correctness** on proof/conceptual arms â€” else the wave HALTs.\n- **P9 write-ordering** is a real hazard: counter-persist is ordered *before* artifact validity; a crash-mid-mint fixture must leave no replayable nonce. Wave 2 round-trips the durable counter across a simulated reload *before* Wave 4 relies on it (so Wave-4's replay test can't pass against an in-memory stub).\n- Required-before-build residuals (A0.5a / R1 / Metric-G+baseline / S1 / S4 / P3 / P7 / P9 + the win32 subprocess & inherited-module contract) are **pinned in DESCRIPTION.md Â§Residuals** with value Â· owner Â· terminus-acceptance. **P8 is deferred to Increment-2.**\n\n**Honesty stamps carried from Stage-1 convergence**\n- `cross_model:false  verified:true` â€” single-family Sharks/Judge. Single-family ceiling = **CLAIMED** on proof/conceptual claims; the correlated-blind-spot register is **FLAGGED, not mitigated**. Autonomous-VERIFIED is re-execution-backed literal computation only; single-process forgery-resistance is best-effort (the warrant is the canary's out-of-band re-execution, not an in-process key).\n\n**Next step (not in this wave list)**\n- Increment-2 / Phase F (F0 environment+integrity probe â†’ F1 cross-family model verifier â†’ F2 Lean â†’ F3 SMT certifier â†’ F4 autonomous dispatch â†’ F5 human gate) builds **only on explicit user promotion**; its full pinned plan is *\"the next Crucible/Foreman pass.\"*\n\nWant me to relay this to Foreman to start the Wave-1 build, or is this purely a documentation handoff?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"c